[CENTER][SIZE=7][B]OptimizeServer[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Performance engineering, bottleneck diagnostics, and safe execution optimization for Minecraft servers.[/SIZE]
[I]by NotGamerPratham[/I]

[URL='https://modrinth.com/plugin/optimizeserver']Modrinth[/URL] | [URL='https://github.com/NotGamerPratham/OptimzeServer/releases']GitHub Releases[/URL] | [URL='https://github.com/NotGamerPratham/OptimzeServer']Source Code[/URL][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]What is OptimizeServer?[/B][/SIZE]
OptimizeServer helps your server run its normal workload more efficiently. It finds bottlenecks, cuts down on unnecessary monitoring overhead, and gives you diagnostics backed by real measurements. [B]It does not change vanilla gameplay.[/B]

[SIZE=5][B]Gameplay Preservation Guarantee[/B][/SIZE]
OptimizeServer [B]never[/B]:
[LIST]
[*]skips ticks or fakes TPS readings
[*]removes entities or disables mob AI
[*]reduces view or simulation distance
[*]forces System.gc() or silently changes world configuration
[/LIST]
Redstone, mob AI, spawning, world generation, chunk loading, combat, and physics all behave exactly as in vanilla.

[SIZE=5][B]Features[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Real-time monitoring:[/B] TPS and MSPT over 5s, 30s, 1m, 5m, and 15m windows (P50/P95/P99), plus CPU, memory/GC, network RTT, chunks, entities, tasks, and storage
[*][B]Diagnostics engine:[/B] classifies bottlenecks as CPU, memory, GC, chunks, entities, plugin tasks, storage, or network, with recommendations backed by evidence
[*][B]Reversible optimizations:[/B] 9 internal modules with before/after measurements and one-command rollback
[*][B]Folia support:[/B] a dedicated scheduler layer for global-region, region, entity, and async tasks
[*][B]Spark & Chunky integration:[/B] if Spark and Chunky are missing, they are downloaded automatically and checked with SHA-512 before installing
[*][B]Local reports:[/B] diagnostic reports are saved on your server, and no data is sent to external services
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Compatibility[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Platforms:[/B] Spigot, Paper, Purpur, Pufferfish, Airplane, Folia, Leaves, Gale (unknown forks run in conservative safe mode)
[*][B]Minecraft:[/B] 1.8.8 – 1.21.x+
[*][B]Java:[/B] 8, 11, 16, 17, 21, 25+
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Commands[/B][/SIZE]
Main command: [B]/optimizeserver[/B] (alias [B]/os[/B])
[LIST]
[*]/os status | tps | mspt | cpu | memory | network | entities
[*]/os chunks [status|recommend|start|pause|cancel]
[*]/os diagnose [full|cpu|memory|chunks|entities|plugins]
[*]/os profile <start|stop|status|memory> | /os health
[*]/os optimize [status|list|enable|disable|rollback]
[*]/os report <generate|history> | /os reload | /os version | /os help
[/LIST]
All permissions fall under [B]optimizeserver.admin[/B] and default to op.

[SIZE=5][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop [B]OptimizeServer.jar[/B] into your [I]plugins/[/I] folder.
[*]Restart the server. If Spark and Chunky are missing, they are installed automatically.
[*]Edit [I]plugins/OptimizeServer/config.yml[/I] if you need to.
[/LIST]

